    "reviewed_findings": [
      "All 65 fixed-scope file hashes match the supplied scope. The reviewed set contains the 18 Thrust formal pages, current canonical/configuration and frozen author research, image/UI/RAW receipts, map/reverse indexes, and the accepted common-mechanism cache.",
      "The player page correctly states the actual windup-event trigger, three effective stacks, action-time cadence with at most one event per fixed update, delayed stat-cache visibility, action/wield/sweep clearing and sweep retention. It distinguishes pure push from melee power input and presents the special toggle separately from model-specific special windups.",
      "The Mk VI dedicated push-combo heavy route, Mk III right-light push-combo route (.45 action-time entry, .5 event threshold, optional early light interruption and later cache-visible retained stack), and Mk IV lack of those dedicated routes are described distinctly. This avoids generalizing one model path to the others.",
      "The two controlled power-input examples recalculate correctly: 500×(1+0+3×.20)=800; and 500×(1+.20)=600 versus 500×(1+.20+2×.10)=700, a 16.67% relative increase to that input only. The pages do not present these as equal final-health-damage increases.",
      "The same-hash English and Traditional Chinese RAW templates are preserved and rebuilt at I–IV from the formatter; the comparison calls omitted action, held, clear, and input-math details “未涵蓋” rather than fabricating a RAW contradiction. Own-tier receipts confirm all 12 actual variants use .05/.10/.15/.20 per effective stack with a three-stack cap.",
      "The actual shared map has one Thrust blessing, 12 variants, and 32 bindings, all binding references resolve to those variants. The metadata-only Thunderhammer candidate is excluded and is not presented as usable. Actual UI/model names, reverse weapon pages, and image path versus attachment are consistent with their fixed receipts; image receipt reports verified public bytes and display review.",
      "Formatting-only follow-up: all 11 affected formal variant pages match the delta receipt after removing exactly one doubled CR before LF; each currently has zero CRCRLF sequences and no visible-text changes are reported by the complete delta proof.",
      "Canonical and extension draft variant_notes are identical and use LF line breaks. The 68-file fixed scope hashes all match; the three added records preserve the earlier accepted scope/peer and document this exact normalization. No mechanics, RAW text, tier values, bindings, formulas, or image data changed."
